-- Review of smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: an act that applies a function local to
-- the rule, an input (`applied`) or a WHERE local (`where positional`,
-- `where named`). The what-if cannot supply a function, and the replay
-- cannot resolve it, so the act is untried with the what-if's own reason;
-- on unstable it was untried with "Internal error: f is not in scope.
-- Please report this as a bug." `plain` and `where plain` are the controls:
-- a local named as a value keeps "the action binds `n`, which the what-if
-- cannot choose".

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`double` x MEANS x TIMES 2

GIVEN f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`applied duty` f MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay (f 3) WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`applied` MEANS `applied duty` `double`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`plain duty` n MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay n WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`plain` MEANS `plain duty` (3 PLUS 3)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`where positional` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST pay (`twice` 3) WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
  WHERE
    GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    `twice` y MEANS y TIMES 2

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`where named` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST pay (`twice` WITH y IS 3) WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
  WHERE
    GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
    GIVETH A NUMBER
    `twice` y MEANS y TIMES 2

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`where plain` MEANS
    PARTY Alice MUST pay six WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
  WHERE
    six MEANS 3 TIMES 2

#TRACE `applied` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES pay 6 AT 1

#TRACE `plain` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES pay 6 AT 1

#TRACE `where positional` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES pay 6 AT 1

#TRACE `where named` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES pay 6 AT 1

#TRACE `where plain` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Alice DOES pay 6 AT 1
